  },
  {
    "name": "agent_archive",
    "description": "Archive a coding agent's session (from agents_list) when the user asks to archive or tidy up agents: it leaves the Agents list for Archived in the app, nothing is deleted, and agent_unarchive brings it back (never remove a session any other way). Persona also asks the agent's own tool to archive it where that tool has an archive (Codex); the result says whether it did (native: done / pending / unsupported). Without close the agent itself is not closed: one open on its computer stays open. With close, its agent and its terminal tab are also closed on its computer (its transcript stays; then it is stopped until resumed): only when the user asks to close it too, and the user confirms on the phone first (declined: nothing changes). A busy agent is refused and nothing changes: working, waiting for an answer or background work, and for close also a /loop, queued messages or a server it runs. When the close does not happen the session stays archived and still open on the computer, and the result says why: tell the user exactly that, not that it was closed. With `force: true`, explicitly cancel and close an Agent stuck waiting for a terminal confirmation, then archive it, as `paseo archive --force` does. Use force only when the user asks to stop or archive that blocked Agent. Pending permissions and plans are rejected or cancelled, never allowed. Working Agents, background work, running subagents/workflows, queued messages, loops and serving ports are still refused. A failed close leaves it visible. Force implies close and does not ask for a second permission card. Not for Persona conversations (conversation_archive).",
    "input_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "machine",
        "session_id"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "machine": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "the machine's id or name, as agents_list shows it"
        },
        "session_id": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "the agent's session id, or its first 8 characters"
        },
        "force": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "description": "cancel and close a confirmation-blocked Agent before archiving; only when the user asks; never approve its pending request"
        },
        "close": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "description": "also close its agent on the computer (asks the user on the phone first); default false: archive only"
        }
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "name": "agent_unarchive",
    "description": "Bring an archived coding agent's session back into the Agents list (find it with agents_list and state archived). Nothing is reopened on the computer: a stopped agent stays stopped until resumed (agent_send with resume). Persona also asks the agent's own tool to restore it where that tool archived it too; the result says whether it did.",
