          "description": "in a sentence, why this answer (kept with the task's decision)"
        }
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "name": "ask_escalate",
    "description": "Hand the cards a task's agents wait on to the user, when a 督办 message gave them to you first and only the user can decide: a form or secret; an approval that sends or replies in their name, spends money or deletes; a question that is irreversible, seen by others, changes the goal or contradicts a decision made on the task. Other permissions and plans are yours (interaction_answer); no card reaches the user on a timeout. Every card of the task the user has not been told of goes to them at once, as one reminder (with push grading on it pushes only for why_owner or p0), with your reason and recommendation; their answers go to the agents and are kept as the task's decisions. Only the task's supervisor and main can; main is told of a leader's escalation, so don't ask the user again.",
    "input_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "todo_id",
        "reason"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "todo_id": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "the task's todo id (todo_…), from the 督办 message"
        },
        "reason": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "in a sentence, in the user's language: what they are to decide and why it is theirs"
        },
        "recommend": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "the option you recommend, in a line (an option's label when there is one)"
        },
        "why_owner": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "irreversible",
            "visible_to_others",
            "priority",
            "acceptance",
            "only_owner_knows"
          ],
          "description": "why only the user can decide it. In the user's push grading only irreversible, visible_to_others and only_owner_knows push to their phone; the rest wait in their Needs you list and briefing"
        },
        "p0": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "description": "true: the user must do or decide this themselves now, so it pushes even in push grading whatever why_owner says"
        }
      }
    },
    "defer_loading": true
  },
  {
    "name": "inbox_suggest",
    "description": "Submit the event’s recap and one suggestion (replaces any earlier one). Nothing goes out until the user confirms; the program executes it verbatim. `kind`: `reply` — message in the user's voice ready to send (no 【…】 blanks; omit unknowns and explain in `note`; to really `@` someone in a connector that supports mentions such as Feishu, pass `mentions` as `[{\"id\":\"\u003cverified user id\u003e\",\"name\":\"\u003cexact display name\u003e\"}]` from the source's search/member tool and write `@name` verbatim in `text` — `@name` without `mentions` is ordinary text; Feishu sheet/Base `changes`: ref, field, listed value); `agent` — new Agent instruction in `text` (`machine`, `cwd` optional); `handoff` — hand to an existing eligible conversation on this manager (main, active leader, or linked task) with `machine`, `session`, and `text` as the note (processing chat only; refuses archived, unknown, or other-manager targets); `todo` — to-do title in `text` (action-led, no chat/people names), `due` only for an explicit deadline (`2006-01-02` all day or RFC 3339 with offset; omit if unsure and note why; confirming files the row); `conclusion` — dealt with, `text` conclusion, `outcome` `fyi` or `done`. `handback: true` returns confirmation here as an instruction for user judgment. `note`: 1–2 sentences on findings/evidence. `recap`: background, progress, blockers (≤600 chars) every time. `title` (no chat/person names) and `summary` (1 sentence on state and who waits) every time; source-titled items (mail, docs, PRs/issues) ignore `title`. `related`: ids of related items in other chats/sources. `recap` without `kind` creates no suggestion and may include `title`, `summary`, and `follow`. `follow` (valid only without `kind`) waits on the other side: `who` (empty = other side's reply), `next`, `check_at` (RFC 3339 with zone) or `check_in` (`30m`, `4h`, `2d`; default `24h`, clamped 30m–14d). `reported`: `{text, by}` records one completed external action unobserved by the program (never plans; `by` `agent`|`assistant`, default `assistant`; one line ≤120 chars; refused on filed items; deduped against latest). Call at end of turn. In a handed-off chat (context names event id), pass `item` to write back (also shown as a card); refuses unhanded or filed items.",
    "input_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "processing_turn": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "item": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "kind": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "reply",
            "agent",
            "handoff",
            "conclusion",
            "todo"
          ]
        },
        "text": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "note": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "handback": {
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "outcome": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "fyi",
            "done"
          ]
        },
        "recap": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "reported": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
            "text"
          ],
          "properties": {
            "text": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "by": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "agent",
                "assistant"
              ],
              "default": "assistant"
            }
          }
        },
        "title": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "summary": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "follow": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "who": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "next": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "check_at": {
              "type": "string",
              "format": "date-time"
            },
            "check_in": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        },
        "machine": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "session": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "cwd": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "due": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "related": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "mentions": {
          "type": "array",
          "maxItems": 100,
          "items": {
            "type": "object",
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "required": [
              "id",
              "name"
            ],
            "properties": {
              "id": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "name": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "changes": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "ref",
              "field",
              "value"
            ],
            "properties": {
              "ref": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "field": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "value": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "defer_loading": true
  },
  {
    "name": "inbox_draft",
    "description": "Legacy inbox_suggest `reply`. Prefer inbox_suggest. Draft a reply for this conversation’s inbox item. It waits in the user's inbox; they read it and send it with one tap (you never send it yourself). `text` is the reply in the user's voice, ready to go out as it is: no blanks to fill in (【…】) — leave out what you could not find and say so in `note`; `note` is one or two sentences on what you found and where, for the user to check the draft against. For a Feishu sheet / Base item, `changes` proposes moving rows' status (ref, field and one of the values the item lists); they are made when the user sends. Call it once, at the end.",
    "input_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "text"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "processing_turn": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "text": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "note": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "changes": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "ref",
              "field",
              "value"
            ],
            "properties": {
              "ref": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "field": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "value": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "defer_loading": true
  },
  {
    "name": "inbox_folders",
    "description": "List the folders the user's inbox items are filed under: each `/`-separated path (`work/alerts/engine`, every segment a level) with its item count and open count, and whether automatic filing by the triage model is on. Give `folder` to also list the items filed in that folder and below, or `unfiled: true` for the items in no folder; each line has the item's id (what inbox_move takes), source, title, sender and whether it is done. Call it before inbox_move, to reuse a folder in use rather than open a near-duplicate.",
    "input_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "folder": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "a folder path: also list the items filed there and below"
        },
        "unfiled": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "description": "also list the items in no folder"
        }
      }
    },
    "defer_loading": true
  },
  {
    "name": "inbox_move",
    "description": "Move inbox items into a folder, as the user would from the inbox: `items` are their ids (from inbox_folders, or the id of an item handed to this conversation), `folder` a `/`-separated path (`work/alerts/engine`; a new path makes the folder), or `\"\"` to take them out of every folder. Moved items stay where they are put: the triage model no longer files them. An unknown id or a path with no name in it moves nothing. Move only what the user asked for.",
    "input_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "items",
        "folder"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "items": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "description": "inbox item ids"
        },
        "folder": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "the folder path, or \"\" for no folder"
        }
      }
    },
    "defer_loading": true
  },
  {
    "name": "inbox_post",
    "description": "Put this conversation into the user's Inbox as a row that opens it, so a result is not missed behind a quiet unread dot. Call it only when the user explicitly asked for it (for example \"tell me if there is anything worth a look\", \"send me the briefing every time\") or when the scheduled task you are running is set to put findings in the Inbox. Never decide on your own to interrupt the user: an ordinary reply, a run with nothing new, or something merely interesting does not go there. `title` is a short name for the row (the task's name or what was found), `summary` one or two sentences saying what to look at, `tier` is `action` when the user has to do something and `fyi` (the default) when it is worth knowing, and `reason` names the request or task setting that makes this post (the user can read it on the row). Calling it again for this conversation soon after updates the same row instead of adding another. It does not push to the phone: use notify_user for that when the user asked for a push.",
    "input_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "title",
        "summary",
        "reason"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "title": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "summary": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "tier": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "action",
            "fyi"
          ]
        },
        "reason": {
          "type": "string"
        }
      }
    },
    "defer_loading": true
  },
  {
    "name": "message_send",
    "description": "Send Lark text (default bot), not via CLI/ask_user. Use a revocable channel/chat/scenario/identity grant or owner approval. Repository grants do not apply. If bot cannot send, report it without changing identity. Reuse idempotency_key on retries. Check destination after uncertain delivery. Other approvals stay.",
    "input_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "channel": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "larkcli"
          ]
        },
        "target": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "oc_ chat ID; resolve read-only."
        },
        "text": {
          "type": "string",
          "minLength": 1,
          "description": "Maximum 16000 UTF-8 bytes."
        },
        "idempotency_key": {
          "type": "string",
          "minLength": 1,
          "maxLength": 200
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "channel",
        "target",
        "text",
        "idempotency_key"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false
    },
    "defer_loading": true
  },
  {
    "name": "kb_search",
    "description": "Search the knowledge base: summaries and metadata of chats, people, projects, docs, meetings, events, recordings (with their minutes and any transcript still retained), topics (curated knowledge points: how something works, what was decided and why, the steps and pitfalls), project timelines, the notes directories the user added (hits with an absolute path) and, with messages=true, the full message archive (newest days first). All words must match. Hits come in the order the files are read, not by relevance, so a broad search can fill the limit with chats: give kind to search one kind only, the entries whose name matches first, then as kb_list ranks them. A past meeting (its decisions, what is still open, who does what) is kind=recordings: found by its title, the calendar event's title, its minutes or any transcript still retained; then kb_get it. Transcripts expire before minutes: never promise a trimmed recording's full transcript.",
    "input_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "query"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "query": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "kind": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "projects",
            "chats",
            "people",
            "docs",
            "meetings",
            "events",
            "recordings",
            "topics"
          ],
          "description": "only this kind's entries (no notes directories; the message archive only with chats)"
        },
        "messages": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "description": "also search the message archive (default true)"
        },
        "limit": {
          "type": "integer",
          "description": "default 40"
        }
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "name": "kb_list",
    "description": "List knowledge-base entities of one kind ranked by importance (P0 first), relevance to the user, recency: projects (short = a feature / launch, long = a team mission), chats, people, docs, meetings, events, recordings (the user's phone / watch recordings; newest first, saying which have meeting minutes, which are all-day recordings with a day recap and its state, and which transcripts have expired), topics (knowledge points curated by subject out of the timelines and chats: concepts, decisions with their reasons, practices, pitfalls, facts, open questions; the biggest first). Transcripts stay for recording_text_days, minutes and recaps for minutes_days (both forever by default). Meetings, events and recordings show when they started, in the user's time zone. Optional tag filter.",
    "input_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "kind"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "kind": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "projects",
            "chats",
            "people",
            "docs",
            "meetings",
            "events",
            "recordings",
            "topics"
          ]
        },
        "tag": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "limit": {
          "type": "integer",
          "description": "default 30"
        }
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "name": "kb_get",
    "description": "Read one entity: its metadata (links to people / chats / projects, tags), compressed context (summary.md), a project's timeline, parent, sub-projects and milestones, a chat's messages of the last 7 days, a recording's meeting minutes, or an all-day recording's day recap (the day's timeline, meetings, suggested to-dos), with each action item's state (suggested, or its to-do's) and its timestamped transcript while still retained (phone/watch recordings, text only), a meeting's / event's recordings, a topic's knowledge points by subtopic (each with its kind, reason and the entries it came from). Transcripts stay for recording_text_days, minutes and recaps for minutes_days (both forever by default). id from kb_list / kb_search (a project also by name). A project lists its 20 most relevant people and a count (all: meta.json).",
    "input_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "kind",
        "id"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "kind": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "projects",
            "chats",
            "people",
            "docs",
            "meetings",
            "events",
            "recordings",
            "topics"
          ]
        },
        "id": {
          "type": "string"
        }
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "name": "kb_update",
    "description": "Write settled facts to the KB. Projects: the fields below (dirs: `\u003cmachine\u003e:\u003cpath\u003e`, linking Agents); merge_into folds a duplicate, unmerge reverses it, each alone in its call. Other kinds take annotations; recordings (phone-owned) only tags, pinned, projects; topics only name, note, aliases, tags. Explicit tags beat automatic ones. remove_* (ids) unlinks only that link, for good. At the user's word only: parent (\"\" = top level); milestone adds (no id), edits or removes (id, remove) a flag; its result has the undo. project_mode/source_urls: reference-only keeps pointers and aliases, details stay at the source; full, alone, restores detail writes.",
    "input_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "kind",
        "id"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "kind": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "projects",
            "chats",
            "people",
            "docs",
            "meetings",
            "events",
            "recordings",
            "topics"
          ]
        },
        "id": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "id, or a project's name (created when new)"
        },
        "merge_into": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "projects: fold into this target (slug or name)"
        },
        "unmerge": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "description": "projects: undo its merge"
        },
        "parent": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "milestone": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "id": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "title": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "target": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "YYYY-MM-DD"
            },
            "state": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "open",
                "accepted",
                "not_accepted"
              ]
            },
            "remove": {
              "type": "boolean"
            }
          }
        },
        "name": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "project_kind": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "short",
            "long"
          ]
        },
        "project_mode": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "full",
            "reference-only"
          ],
          "description": "user-directed"
        },
        "source_urls": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "description": "user-directed; replace; empty list clears"
        },
        "status": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "active",
            "paused",
            "done"
          ]
        },
        "goal": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "my_role": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "note": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "importance": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "P0",
            "P1",
            "P2",
            "P3"
          ]
        },
        "relevance": {
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "tags": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "summary": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Markdown, replaces summary.md"
        },
        "log": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "one line appended to a project's timeline"
        },
        "aliases": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "remove_aliases": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "description": "projects: aliases that are not this project's (another's name, too generic)"
        },
        "chats": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "remove_chats": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "people": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "remove_people": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "dirs": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "projects": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "name": "kb_history_plan",
    "description": "Show or change what a source's history import reads. What is read of each chat comes from the knowledge base's selection (the same rules as daily ingestion; per-chat settings are changed here with `set`): the whole chat, only the user's own messages (with the messages around them) and mentions of the user, or nothing. Without `set` or `back_days` it refreshes the source's chat list and lists the chats grouped that way, largest first, with each chat's id and any per-chat setting of the user's. `set` changes per-chat settings, which apply to daily ingestion too: a chat by its id or exact name (a name two chats share is refused with their ids, a name no chat has gets close names; then nothing is changed); `read: false` never reads it, `read: true, store: true` keeps the whole chat (for `days`, or as the rules say), `read: true, store: false` only the user's messages and mentions, `reset: true` back to the rules. `back_days` limits how far back the import goes (null: as far as the rules keep messages). A change, or a refreshed list, that reads more than the user approved takes the approval back, so the import needs kb_history_resume again; reading less does not. Listing or changing never starts the import: show the user the list, apply the exceptions they name, show the result again, and only when they say to start call kb_history_resume. Needs `kb.history.enabled` in manager.json.",
    "input_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "source": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "connector id from kb.history.sources; omitted: every configured source (required with set or back_days)"
        },
        "set": {
          "type": "array",
          "description": "per-chat settings to change, all or none",
          "items": {
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "chat"
            ],
            "properties": {
              "chat": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "the chat's id, or its exact name"
              },
              "read": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "description": "false: never read it (required unless reset)"
              },
              "store": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "description": "true: keep the whole chat; false: only the user's messages and mentions"
              },
              "days": {
                "type": [
                  "integer",
                  "null"
                ],
                "description": "with store: how many days its lines are kept (null: as the rules say)"
              },
              "reset": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "description": "remove the chat's setting: the rules decide again"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "back_days": {
          "type": [
            "integer",
            "null"
          ],
          "description": "how many days back the import goes for this source; null: as far as the rules keep messages"
        }
      }
    },
    "defer_loading": true
  },
  {
    "name": "kb_history_status",
    "description": "How the history import is doing, per source: its state (running, resting, paused, stopped, done, waiting for approval or for the search index), whether its plan is approved, chats done / to go / paused / in error / unreadable with messages read and written, calls and messages in the last hour, the last slowdown, pause and stop with their reasons, and the last call. Read-only.",
    "input_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "source": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "one connector id; omitted: all configured sources"
        }
      }
    },
    "defer_loading": true
  },
  {
    "name": "kb_history_stop",
    "description": "Stop the history import now: it makes no further call until the user resumes it (the call in flight, if any, finishes; nothing is cancelled). Use it whenever the user says to stop or pause importing history.",
    "input_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "reason": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "why, in a few words, as the user said it; shown in the status, never written to the log"
        }
      }
    },
    "defer_loading": true
  },
  {
    "name": "kb_history_resume",
    "description": "Approve a source's history import plan, as the selection reads it now, and start or resume the import (it also clears a stop). Only when the user has seen the plan (kb_history_plan) and explicitly says to start or resume; never on your own. After a stop, check kb_history_status first and tell the user why it stopped; `slow` keeps the slowest pace for the first two hours after the import starts again, the safe choice after a stop.",
    "input_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "source"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "source": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "connector id from kb.history.sources"
        },
        "slow": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "description": "the slowest pace for the first two hours of calls"
        }
      }
    },
    "defer_loading": true
  },
  {
    "name": "persona_settings",
    "description": "Read and change Persona's settings: inbox sorting and task links, 关于我, default launcher, mail accounts, machine Claude Code exclusions and extensions. List keys and inputs; get reads one. set/add/remove show before → after on the phone and wait for approval; secrets are entered there, never requested in chat. Change only what was asked.\n\nModel groups `model_config.kb`, `model_config.inbox.triage`, `model_config.agent.delegate` and `model_config.translate`: `get` returns their effective binding, revision and compatible `purpose.provider_ids`. `set` and `test` take one listed provider ID as value. A changed provider clears the old model, effort and permission mode. `test` only checks the connection, without approval or saving; an unverified or offline provider may still be saved.\n\n`assistant.standing_authorizations`: only the main conversation may replace the list at its current revision with the user’s phone approval. Each grant names `machine_id`, absolute `directory`, `actions` (merge, push, deploy-test, deploy-production, send, delete, spend), `conditions`, exact user `quote`, `source` and `reversible`. Keep unchanged grants by ID; replace one by removing it and adding it without an ID. Never invent a quote or expand scope. Only independently verifiable conditions may permit automatic answers. Revoke in Settings. Tool permissions are never automatically approved.",
    "input_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "action": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "list",
            "get",
            "set",
            "test",
            "add",
            "remove"
          ],
          "description": "default list"
        },
        "key": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "the setting, from list (inbox.rules, mail.accounts, extension.\u003cid\u003e…)"
        },
        "value": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "number",
            "integer",
            "boolean",
            "object",
