  {
    "name": "secret_run",
    "description": "Run commands on one of the user's computers with a password only the user knows, for sudo or one-off LAN/CLI auth. Never ask in chat or ask_user. The card lists the computer, purpose and commands verbatim and needs a fresh password and Run every time (no remembered/quick approval or Watch). The node runs only those commands in order with /bin/sh -c in the home directory and PATH=/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin (other tools need absolute paths). Commands are printable ASCII; the first failure stops.\n\ndelivery=stdin (default): only a command running one sudo -S gets the password and a newline on stdin; every other command gets empty stdin. Write sudo as `sudo -S -k -p '' …`, never after a pipe or without -S. With NOPASSWD, sudo does not read stdin and its command may read the password instead, so give that command no stdin reader.\n\ndelivery=env: explicit one-off non-sudo authentication. Every command gets the password in its PERSONA_SECRET environment and empty stdin, never in argv. The card warns that encoded output can evade literal redaction, so every command must be safe for the user to trust with the secret. Env requires the node's secret_run_env capability; an older node refuses during preflight before the user types anything. Not on Windows.\n\nNever print, store or send the password; you never see it. Result JSON: status (ran, failed, declined, expired or refused), computer, message and, for ran/failed, each exit_code, timed_out and clipped output. Literal password in output withholds it whole (output_withheld). A timeout may leave a root process: check before retrying. Declined, expired and refused mean nothing ran: tell the user and retry only if wanted.",
    "input_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "machine",
        "purpose",
        "commands"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "machine": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "the computer to run on: its id or name, as agent_start takes it"
        },
        "purpose": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "one sentence the card shows: why the password is needed"
        },
        "commands": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "minItems": 1,
          "maxItems": 5,
          "description": "1 to 5 one-line shell commands of printable ASCII, at most 1000 characters each, run in order"
        },
        "delivery": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "stdin",
            "env"
          ],
          "description": "stdin (default): sudo -S only; env: PERSONA_SECRET for one-off non-sudo commands"
        },
        "timeout_seconds": {
          "type": "integer",
          "minimum": 1,
          "maximum": 1800,
          "description": "for the whole run, default 300"
        }
      },
      "additionalProperties": false
    },
    "defer_loading": true
  },
  {
    "name": "skill_import",
    "description": "Import a user-requested skill ZIP through Persona's existing Settings importer. First preview the base64-encoded archive (up to 4 MiB compressed); returns validated metadata, a short-lived reference and environment. Then install with the same archive, reference and environment. Installation and undo wait for the user's own permission card showing the validated skill and target computer; never approve for the user. The target is the current assistant's configured personal computer, never a model-chosen path or machine. Skills are shared by assistants using that computer account and load in new conversations; an existing conversation is not guaranteed to refresh. Same-name skills are never overwritten. ZIP inspection does not run scripts or treat skill instructions as authorization. Use status with the original reference and environment after a lost/uncertain response, before any retry: it records previewed, installed or undone and recovers the undo receipt. Status is an operation receipt, not a live inventory; receipts expire after ten minutes or a computer restart. If unavailable, inspect Settings \u003e Skills instead of assuming failure. Cancel discards an unused preview. Undo takes an installed receipt, refuses edited/replaced files and retains recovery data. No URL download, repository clone, arbitrary path write or arbitrary skill removal is provided. An older computer may require a Persona update.",
